From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gdi32, spoolss, unidrvui, wineumpd: makers' print processors place and order pages as on Windows

Lexmark's print processor sent the last page first, and its pages and
HP's sat off where winprint puts them:

- spoolss: GetJobAttributes asks the printer's configuration DLL
  (DrvQueryJobAttributes, ATTRIBUTE_INFO_3), as Windows does; it made up
  zeros. A processor opened with the port's name ("port, Port") has the
  printer's name in the job's devmode.
- unidrvui: DrvQueryJobAttributes (Microsoft Learn): one page per side,
  the processor makes the copies, the job's page order from the GPD's page
  order feature (ReverseOrderPrinting/JobPageOrder), and the driver orders
  pages itself when the GPD has such a feature. Lexmark's processor sends
  the pages in order then.
- gdi32: a spooled page's EMF frame is a sheet's size from the printable
  area's origin, and GdiPlayPageEMF with no (or an empty) rectangle plays
  into that: HP's processor plays into the sheet from the origin, and
  Lexmark's into (0,0)-(DESKTOPHORZRES,DESKTOPVERTRES). This replaces 1041's
  frame around the origin, which put HP's page off by the printable
  offset.
- wineumpd: a printer DC's DESKTOPHORZRES/DESKTOPVERTRES are the sheet's
  size (they were 0), which Lexmark's processor sizes the page by.

HP through its processor and Lexmark through its processor now print
their pages where and in the order winprint does (ink boxes within
0.05 in).

Test: test/drvui-gate.sh (mutants SG_MUTANT_DRVORDER, QUERYJOBATTR),
test/printdrv-gate.sh (DESKTOPRES), test/printproc-gate.sh (SPOOLFRAME,
PLAYSHEET, EMPTYRECT).
---
--- a/dlls/gdi32/dc.c
+++ b/dlls/gdi32/dc.c
@@ -3309,13 +3309,12 @@
 #endif
     if (!document)
     {
-        /* the whole sheet around the printable area's origin, as the page's
+        /* a sheet's size from the printable area's origin, as the page's
          * frame is (spool_start_page) */
-        int off_x = GetDeviceCaps( sh->hdc, PHYSICALOFFSETX ), off_y = GetDeviceCaps( sh->hdc, PHYSICALOFFSETY );
         int width = GetDeviceCaps( sh->hdc, PHYSICALWIDTH ), height = GetDeviceCaps( sh->hdc, PHYSICALHEIGHT );
 
 #ifndef SG_MUTANT_PLAYSHEET
-        if (width && height) SetRect( &full, -off_x, -off_y, width - off_x, height - off_y );
+        if (width && height) SetRect( &full, 0, 0, width, height );
         else
 #endif
         SetRect( &full, 0, 0, GetDeviceCaps( sh->hdc, HORZRES ), GetDeviceCaps( sh->hdc, VERTRES ) );
